/-!
# The relative Grothendieck group of a functor

For a functor `T : C ⥤ D` out of a category with zero morphisms and binary biproducts -- an
additive functor between additive categories, in the intended application -- the relative group
`TauCeti.RelativeK0 T`, written `K₀(T)`, is the abelian group generated by the triples
`(P, α, Q)` of objects `P`, `Q` of `C` and an isomorphism `α : T(P) ≅ T(Q)` in `D`, written
`[P, α, Q]`, subject to

* isomorphism invariance: `[P, α, Q] = [P', α', Q']` whenever there are isomorphisms
  `f : P ≅ P'` and `g : Q ≅ Q'` with `T(f) ≫ α' = α ≫ T(g)`;
* direct sums: `[P ⊞ P', γ, Q ⊞ Q'] = [P, α, Q] + [P', α', Q']` whenever `γ` restricts to `α` and
  `α'` along `T` of the two inclusions;
* composition: `[P, α, Q] + [Q, β, S] = [P, α ≫ β, S]`.

When `T` preserves binary biproducts the isomorphism `γ` of the direct-sum relation is exactly
`α ⊞ α'` transported along `T(P ⊞ P') ≅ T(P) ⊞ T(P')` (`TauCeti.RelativeK0.of_biprod`).
The difference map `[P, α, Q] ↦ [P] - [Q]` (`TauCeti.RelativeK0.toSplitK0`) lands in the split
Grothendieck group of `C`, and an automorphism `α` of an object `T(P)` has a class `[P, α, P]`.
For base change from finitely generated projective `R`-modules to `R/I`-modules, `K₀(T)` is the
relative group `K₀(R, I)` of a two-sided ideal `I`, the middle term of the exact sequence
`K₁(R) → K₁(R/I) → K₀(R, I) → K₀(R) → K₀(R/I)`. When `T` sends every object to a zero object the
difference map is an isomorphism (`TauCeti.RelativeK0.toSplitK0EquivOfIsZero`), which gives
`K₀(R, R) ≅ K₀(R)`.

The presentation uses only direct sums, but when `D` is preadditive and `T` preserves binary
biproducts it already satisfies the relation for split short exact sequences of triples
(`TauCeti.RelativeK0.of_eq_add_of_inl_comp_eq_of_comp_snd_eq`): if
`γ : T(P₁ ⊞ P₂) ≅ T(Q₁ ⊞ Q₂)` is triangular, restricting to `α₁` on the first summand and inducing
`α₂` on the second, then
`[P₁ ⊞ P₂, γ, Q₁ ⊞ Q₂] = [P₁, α₁, Q₁] + [P₂, α₂, Q₂]`, whatever its off-diagonal block. That block
need not come from a morphism of `C`: the unipotent automorphism it defines becomes a commutator
after adding a summand
(`CategoryTheory.Biprod.unipotentLower_biprod_eq_commutatorElement`), and commutators have
trivial class because the automorphisms of a fixed `T(P)` contribute additively. This is the
additivity that Weibel's presentation of `K₀(T)` imposes along short exact sequences of triples,
for those sequences which split, as all short exact sequences of finitely generated projective
modules do.

The group is functorial in commuting squares of functors `T ⋙ G ≅ F ⋙ T'`
(`TauCeti.RelativeK0.map`), compatibly with the difference maps
(`TauCeti.RelativeK0.toSplitK0_comp_map`). For a fully faithful `T` every isomorphism
`T(P) ≅ T(Q)` is the image of an isomorphism `P ≅ Q`, so `K₀(T)` vanishes; in particular
`K₀(𝟭 C) = 0`.

No smallness is assumed: `RelativeK0 T` lives in the universe of the objects of `C` and the
morphisms of `D`. Only the difference map, whose target is split `K₀` of `C`, asks for `C` to be
essentially small.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.RelativeK0 T`: the relative group `K₀(T)` of a functor, with class map
  `TauCeti.RelativeK0.of`.
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.Invariant T G`: a function on triples satisfying the three defining
  relations, and `TauCeti.RelativeK0.lift` the homomorphism it induces.
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.toSplitK0`: the difference map `K₀(T) → K₀(C)`.
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.map`: the homomorphism induced by a commuting square of functors.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.of_congr`, `TauCeti.RelativeK0.of_eq_add_of_inl_comp_eq_of_inr_comp_eq`,
  `TauCeti.RelativeK0.of_trans`: the three defining relations.
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.of_refl`, `TauCeti.RelativeK0.of_symm`, `TauCeti.RelativeK0.of_mapIso`:
  `[P, id, P] = 0`, `[Q, α⁻¹, P] = -[P, α, Q]` and `[P, T(γ), Q] = 0`.
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.of_biprod`: the direct-sum relation for a functor preserving binary
  biproducts.
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.of_eq_add_of_inl_comp_eq_of_comp_snd_eq`: the relation for triangular
  isomorphisms.
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.liftEquiv`: the universal property.
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.induction_on`: induction on the classes of triples.
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.exists_eq_of`: every element is the class of a single triple.
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.toSplitK0_of`: the difference map sends `[P, α, Q]` to `[P] - [Q]`.
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.toSplitK0EquivOfIsZero`: the difference map is an isomorphism when `T` sends
  every object to a zero object.
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.subsingleton_of_full_of_faithful`: `K₀(T) = 0` for a fully faithful `T`.
* `TauCeti.RelativeK0.map_id`, `TauCeti.RelativeK0.map_comp`,
  `TauCeti.RelativeK0.toSplitK0_comp_map`: functoriality in commuting squares.

## References

* Charles A. Weibel, *The K-book: An Introduction to Algebraic K-theory*, Chapter II,
  Definition 2.10 (the relative group `K₀(T)` of a functor) and Exercise 2.17.
-/

public section

namespace TauCeti

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits ZeroObject
open scoped commutatorElement

universe w v v' v'' v''' u u' u'' u'''

section Relations

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] [HasZeroMorphisms C] [HasBinaryBiproducts C]
  {D : Type u'} [Category.{v'} D] (T : C ⥤ D)

/-- The defining relations of the relative group `K₀(T)`: isomorphism invariance, additivity under
binary biproducts and additivity under composition, as elements of the free abelian group on all
triples `(P, Q, α : T(P) ≅ T(Q))`. -/
def relativeK0Relations : Set (FreeAddCommGroup (Σ P Q : C, T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q)) :=
  {r | (∃ (P P' Q Q' : C) (f : P ≅ P') (g : Q ≅ Q') (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q)
        (α' : T.obj P' ≅ T.obj Q'), T.map f.hom ≫ α'.hom = α.hom ≫ T.map g.hom ∧
        r = FreeAddCommGroup.of ⟨P', Q', α'⟩ - FreeAddCommGroup.of ⟨P, Q, α⟩) ∨
      (∃ (P P' Q Q' : C) (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) (α' : T.obj P' ≅ T.obj Q')
        (γ : T.obj (P ⊞ P') ≅ T.obj (Q ⊞ Q')),
        T.map biprod.inl ≫ γ.hom = α.hom ≫ T.map biprod.inl ∧
        T.map biprod.inr ≫ γ.hom = α'.hom ≫ T.map biprod.inr ∧
        r = FreeAddCommGroup.of ⟨P ⊞ P', Q ⊞ Q', γ⟩ - FreeAddCommGroup.of ⟨P, Q, α⟩ -
          FreeAddCommGroup.of ⟨P', Q', α'⟩) ∨
      (∃ (P Q S : C) (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) (β : T.obj Q ≅ T.obj S),
        r = FreeAddCommGroup.of ⟨P, S, α ≪≫ β⟩ - FreeAddCommGroup.of ⟨P, Q, α⟩ -
          FreeAddCommGroup.of ⟨Q, S, β⟩)}

variable {T} in
/-- Membership in the defining relations of the relative group `K₀(T)`. -/
theorem mem_relativeK0Relations_iff {r : FreeAddCommGroup (Σ P Q : C, T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q)} :
    r ∈ relativeK0Relations T ↔
      (∃ (P P' Q Q' : C) (f : P ≅ P') (g : Q ≅ Q') (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q)
          (α' : T.obj P' ≅ T.obj Q'), T.map f.hom ≫ α'.hom = α.hom ≫ T.map g.hom ∧
          r = FreeAddCommGroup.of ⟨P', Q', α'⟩ - FreeAddCommGroup.of ⟨P, Q, α⟩) ∨
        (∃ (P P' Q Q' : C) (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) (α' : T.obj P' ≅ T.obj Q')
          (γ : T.obj (P ⊞ P') ≅ T.obj (Q ⊞ Q')),
          T.map biprod.inl ≫ γ.hom = α.hom ≫ T.map biprod.inl ∧
          T.map biprod.inr ≫ γ.hom = α'.hom ≫ T.map biprod.inr ∧
          r = FreeAddCommGroup.of ⟨P ⊞ P', Q ⊞ Q', γ⟩ - FreeAddCommGroup.of ⟨P, Q, α⟩ -
            FreeAddCommGroup.of ⟨P', Q', α'⟩) ∨
        (∃ (P Q S : C) (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) (β : T.obj Q ≅ T.obj S),
          r = FreeAddCommGroup.of ⟨P, S, α ≪≫ β⟩ - FreeAddCommGroup.of ⟨P, Q, α⟩ -
            FreeAddCommGroup.of ⟨Q, S, β⟩) :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- The relative Grothendieck group `K₀(T)` of a functor `T : C ⥤ D`: the abelian group generated
by the classes `[P, α, Q]` of triples of objects `P`, `Q` of `C` and isomorphisms
`α : T(P) ≅ T(Q)`, subject to `[P, α, Q] = [P', α', Q']` for isomorphisms `f : P ≅ P'`,
`g : Q ≅ Q'` with `T(f) ≫ α' = α ≫ T(g)`, `[P ⊞ P', γ, Q ⊞ Q'] = [P, α, Q] + [P', α', Q']` for `γ`
restricting to `α` and `α'` along `T` of the inclusions, and
`[P, α ≫ β, S] = [P, α, Q] + [Q, β, S]`. -/
def RelativeK0 : Type (max u v') :=
  FreeAddCommGroup (Σ P Q : C, T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) ⧸ AddSubgroup.closure (relativeK0Relations T)

instance : AddCommGroup (RelativeK0 T) :=
  inferInstanceAs (AddCommGroup (FreeAddCommGroup (Σ P Q : C, T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) ⧸
    AddSubgroup.closure (relativeK0Relations T)))

end Relations

namespace RelativeK0

section Basic

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] [HasZeroMorphisms C] [HasBinaryBiproducts C]
  {D : Type u'} [Category.{v'} D] (T : C ⥤ D)

/-- The quotient map from the free abelian group on all triples onto `K₀(T)`. -/
private noncomputable def mk : FreeAddCommGroup (Σ P Q : C, T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) →+ RelativeK0 T :=
  QuotientAddGroup.mk' _

private lemma mk_surjective : Function.Surjective (mk T) :=
  QuotientAddGroup.mk'_surjective _

private lemma mk_eq_zero_of_mem {r : FreeAddCommGroup (Σ P Q : C, T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q)}
    (hr : r ∈ relativeK0Relations T) : mk T r = 0 :=
  (QuotientAddGroup.eq_zero_iff r).2 (AddSubgroup.subset_closure hr)

/-- The class `[P, α, Q]` in `K₀(T)` of an isomorphism `α : T(P) ≅ T(Q)`. -/
noncomputable def of {P Q : C} (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) : RelativeK0 T :=
  mk T (FreeAddCommGroup.of ⟨P, Q, α⟩)

private lemma mk_of {P Q : C} (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) :
    mk T (FreeAddCommGroup.of ⟨P, Q, α⟩) = of T α := (rfl)

variable {T}

/-- Isomorphism invariance: triples identified by isomorphisms `f : P ≅ P'` and `g : Q ≅ Q'` with
`T(f) ≫ α' = α ≫ T(g)` have the same class. -/
theorem of_congr {P P' Q Q' : C} (f : P ≅ P') (g : Q ≅ Q') {α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q}
    {α' : T.obj P' ≅ T.obj Q'} (h : T.map f.hom ≫ α'.hom = α.hom ≫ T.map g.hom) :
    of T α = of T α' := by
  have h := mk_eq_zero_of_mem T (Or.inl ⟨P, P', Q, Q', f, g, α, α', h, rfl⟩)
  rwa [map_sub, mk_of, mk_of, sub_eq_zero, eq_comm] at h

/-- The direct-sum relation: if `γ : T(P ⊞ P') ≅ T(Q ⊞ Q')` restricts to `α` and `α'` along `T` of
the two inclusions, then `[P ⊞ P', γ, Q ⊞ Q'] = [P, α, Q] + [P', α', Q']`. -/
theorem of_eq_add_of_inl_comp_eq_of_inr_comp_eq {P P' Q Q' : C} {α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q}
    {α' : T.obj P' ≅ T.obj Q'} {γ : T.obj (P ⊞ P') ≅ T.obj (Q ⊞ Q')}
    (h₁ : T.map biprod.inl ≫ γ.hom = α.hom ≫ T.map biprod.inl)
    (h₂ : T.map biprod.inr ≫ γ.hom = α'.hom ≫ T.map biprod.inr) :
    of T γ = of T α + of T α' := by
  have h := mk_eq_zero_of_mem T (Or.inr (Or.inl ⟨P, P', Q, Q', α, α', γ, h₁, h₂, rfl⟩))
  rwa [map_sub, map_sub, mk_of, mk_of, mk_of, sub_sub, sub_eq_zero] at h

/-- The composition relation: `[P, α ≫ β, S] = [P, α, Q] + [Q, β, S]`. -/
@[simp]
theorem of_trans {P Q S : C} (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) (β : T.obj Q ≅ T.obj S) :
    of T (α ≪≫ β) = of T α + of T β := by
  have h := mk_eq_zero_of_mem T (Or.inr (Or.inr ⟨P, Q, S, α, β, rfl⟩))
  rwa [map_sub, map_sub, mk_of, mk_of, mk_of, sub_sub, sub_eq_zero] at h

/-- The class of an identity triple vanishes: `[P, id, P] = 0`. -/
@[simp]
theorem of_refl (P : C) : of T (Iso.refl (T.obj P)) = 0 := by
  have h := of_trans (Iso.refl (T.obj P)) (Iso.refl (T.obj P))
  rwa [Iso.refl_trans, left_eq_add] at h

/-- Reversing a triple negates its class: `[Q, α⁻¹, P] = -[P, α, Q]`. -/
@[simp]
theorem of_symm {P Q : C} (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) : of T α.symm = -of T α := by
  rw [eq_neg_iff_add_eq_zero, ← of_trans, Iso.symm_self_id, of_refl]

/-- The class of the image of an isomorphism of `C` vanishes: `[P, T(γ), Q] = 0`. -/
@[simp]
theorem of_mapIso {P Q : C} (γ : P ≅ Q) : of T (T.mapIso γ) = 0 := by
  rw [of_congr γ (Iso.refl Q) (α' := Iso.refl (T.obj Q)) (by simp), of_refl]

/-- The class of a commutator of automorphisms of an object of `D` vanishes, once the object is
identified with an image of `T`. -/
theorem of_trans_commutatorElement_trans {P : C} {W : D} (e : T.obj P ≅ W) (a b : Aut W) :
    of T (e ≪≫ (⁅a, b⁆ : Aut W).asIso ≪≫ e.symm) = 0 := by
  have h (x : Aut W) : of T (e ≪≫ x⁻¹.asIso ≪≫ e.symm) = -of T (e ≪≫ x.asIso ≪≫ e.symm) := by
    rw [← of_symm]
    congr 1
    ext
    simp
  have h' (x y : Aut W) : of T (e ≪≫ (x * y).asIso ≪≫ e.symm) =
      of T (e ≪≫ x.asIso ≪≫ e.symm) + of T (e ≪≫ y.asIso ≪≫ e.symm) := by
    rw [add_comm, ← of_trans]
    congr 1
    ext
    simp
  rw [commutatorElement_def, h', h', h', h, h]
  abel

/-- Two homomorphisms out of `K₀(T)` that agree on the classes of all triples are equal. -/
@[ext]
theorem hom_ext {G : Type*} [AddMonoid G] {f g : RelativeK0 T →+ G}
    (h : ∀ (P Q : C) (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q), f (of T α) = g (of T α)) : f = g := by
  refine AddMonoidHom.ext fun x => ?_
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := mk_surjective T x
  induction y using FreeAddCommGroup.induction_on with
  | zero => rw [map_zero, map_zero, map_zero]
  | of p => exact h p.1 p.2.1 p.2.2
  | neg p hp =>
      -- In a monoid, `f (-a)` and `g (-a)` are both inverses of `f a = g a`.
      refine left_neg_eq_right_neg (a := f (mk T (FreeAddCommGroup.of p))) ?_ ?_
      · rw [← map_add, ← map_add, neg_add_cancel, map_zero, map_zero]
      · rw [hp, ← map_add, ← map_add, add_neg_cancel, map_zero, map_zero]
  | add a b ha hb => simp only [map_add, ha, hb]

/-- Induction on the classes of triples. -/
@[elab_as_elim]
theorem induction_on {motive : RelativeK0 T → Prop} (x : RelativeK0 T) (zero : motive 0)
    (of : ∀ (P Q : C) (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q), motive (of T α))
    (add : ∀ a b, motive a → motive b → motive (a + b)) (neg : ∀ a, motive a → motive (-a)) :
    motive x := by
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := mk_surjective T x
  induction y using FreeAddCommGroup.induction_on with
  | zero => rwa [map_zero]
  | of p => exact of p.1 p.2.1 p.2.2
  | neg p hp => simpa only [map_neg] using neg _ hp
  | add a b ha hb => simpa only [map_add] using add _ _ ha hb

variable (T) in
/-- The classes of triples generate `K₀(T)`. -/
theorem closure_range_of :
    AddSubgroup.closure (Set.range fun p : Σ P Q : C, T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q => of T p.2.2) = ⊤ :=
  eq_top_iff.2 fun x _ => induction_on x (zero_mem _)
    (fun P Q α => AddSubgroup.subset_closure ⟨⟨P, Q, α⟩, rfl⟩) (fun _ _ => add_mem)
    (fun _ => neg_mem)

end Basic

section Biprod

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] [HasZeroMorphisms C] [HasBinaryBiproducts C]
  {D : Type u'} [Category.{v'} D] [HasZeroMorphisms D] {T : C ⥤ D} [T.PreservesZeroMorphisms]
  [PreservesBinaryBiproducts T]

/-- The direct-sum relation for a functor preserving binary biproducts:
`[P ⊞ P', α ⊞ α', Q ⊞ Q'] = [P, α, Q] + [P', α', Q']`, where `α ⊞ α'` is transported along
`T(P ⊞ P') ≅ T(P) ⊞ T(P')`. -/
@[simp]
theorem of_biprod {P P' Q Q' : C} (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) (α' : T.obj P' ≅ T.obj Q') :
    of T (T.mapBiprod P P' ≪≫ biprod.mapIso α α' ≪≫ (T.mapBiprod Q Q').symm) =
      of T α + of T α' :=
  of_eq_add_of_inl_comp_eq_of_inr_comp_eq (by simp) (by simp)

/-- Every element of `K₀(T)` is the class of a single triple: sums are realized by biproducts and
negatives by reversing the isomorphism. This needs `C` to be nonempty, so that `0` is the class
of an identity triple. -/
theorem exists_eq_of [Nonempty C] (x : RelativeK0 T) :
    ∃ (P Q : C) (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q), of T α = x := by
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := mk_surjective T x
  induction y using FreeAddCommGroup.induction_on with
  | zero => exact ⟨Classical.arbitrary C, _, Iso.refl _, by rw [of_refl, map_zero]⟩
  | of p => exact ⟨p.1, p.2.1, p.2.2, rfl⟩
  | neg p hp =>
      obtain ⟨P, Q, α, h⟩ := hp
      exact ⟨Q, P, α.symm, by rw [of_symm, h, map_neg]⟩
  | add a b ha hb =>
      obtain ⟨P, Q, α, hα⟩ := ha
      obtain ⟨P', Q', α', hα'⟩ := hb
      refine ⟨P ⊞ P', Q ⊞ Q',
        T.mapBiprod P P' ≪≫ biprod.mapIso α α' ≪≫ (T.mapBiprod Q Q').symm, ?_⟩
      rw [map_add, ← hα, ← hα', of_biprod]

end Biprod

section Triangular

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] [HasZeroMorphisms C] [HasBinaryBiproducts C]
  {D : Type u'} [Category.{v'} D] [Preadditive D] [HasBinaryBiproducts D] {T : C ⥤ D}
  [T.PreservesZeroMorphisms] [PreservesBinaryBiproducts T]

/-- An automorphism of `T(Q₁ ⊞ Q₂)` which fixes `T` of the first summand and induces the identity
on `T` of the second has trivial class, whatever its off-diagonal block. -/
theorem of_eq_zero_of_inl_comp_eq_of_comp_snd_eq {Q₁ Q₂ : C}
    {u : T.obj (Q₁ ⊞ Q₂) ≅ T.obj (Q₁ ⊞ Q₂)}
    (h₁ : T.map biprod.inl ≫ u.hom = T.map biprod.inl)
    (h₂ : u.hom ≫ T.map biprod.snd = T.map biprod.snd) : of T u = 0 := by
  set M := T.mapBiprod Q₁ Q₂
  -- Add the identity triple on `Q₂` and identify `T((Q₁ ⊞ Q₂) ⊞ Q₂)` with
  -- `(T(Q₁) ⊞ T(Q₂)) ⊞ T(Q₂)`, where `u ⊞ 𝟙` becomes a commutator.
  set E : T.obj ((Q₁ ⊞ Q₂) ⊞ Q₂) ≅ (T.obj Q₁ ⊞ T.obj Q₂) ⊞ T.obj Q₂ :=
    T.mapBiprod (Q₁ ⊞ Q₂) Q₂ ≪≫ biprod.mapIso M (Iso.refl _)
  have h : T.mapBiprod (Q₁ ⊞ Q₂) Q₂ ≪≫ biprod.mapIso u (Iso.refl _) ≪≫
      (T.mapBiprod (Q₁ ⊞ Q₂) Q₂).symm =
      E ≪≫ (Aut.of (biprod.mapIso (M.symm ≪≫ u ≪≫ M) (Iso.refl _))).asIso ≪≫ E.symm := by
    have hu : biprod.mapIso u (Iso.refl (T.obj Q₂)) = biprod.mapIso M (Iso.refl _) ≪≫
        biprod.mapIso (M.symm ≪≫ u ≪≫ M) (Iso.refl _) ≪≫ (biprod.mapIso M (Iso.refl _)).symm := by
      ext <;> simp
    rw [hu]
    simp only [E, Iso.trans_symm, Iso.trans_assoc]
  have h' := of_biprod u (Iso.refl (T.obj Q₂))
  rw [of_refl, add_zero, h, T.mapBiprod_symm_trans_trans_eq_unipotentLower u h₁ h₂,
    Biprod.unipotentLower_biprod_eq_commutatorElement, of_trans_commutatorElement_trans] at h'
  exact h'.symm

/-- The relation for triangular isomorphisms: if `γ : T(P₁ ⊞ P₂) ≅ T(Q₁ ⊞ Q₂)` restricts to `α₁`
along `T` of the first inclusions and induces `α₂` along `T` of the second projections, then
`[P₁ ⊞ P₂, γ, Q₁ ⊞ Q₂] = [P₁, α₁, Q₁] + [P₂, α₂, Q₂]`, whatever its off-diagonal block
`T(P₂) ⟶ T(Q₁)`. This is the relation imposed by a split short exact sequence of triples. -/
theorem of_eq_add_of_inl_comp_eq_of_comp_snd_eq {P₁ P₂ Q₁ Q₂ : C} {α₁ : T.obj P₁ ≅ T.obj Q₁}
    {α₂ : T.obj P₂ ≅ T.obj Q₂} {γ : T.obj (P₁ ⊞ P₂) ≅ T.obj (Q₁ ⊞ Q₂)}
    (h₁ : T.map biprod.inl ≫ γ.hom = α₁.hom ≫ T.map biprod.inl)
    (h₂ : γ.hom ≫ T.map biprod.snd = T.map biprod.snd ≫ α₂.hom) :
    of T γ = of T α₁ + of T α₂ := by
  set δ := T.mapBiprod P₁ P₂ ≪≫ biprod.mapIso α₁ α₂ ≪≫ (T.mapBiprod Q₁ Q₂).symm
  have hδ₁ : T.map biprod.inl ≫ δ.inv = α₁.inv ≫ T.map biprod.inl := by simp [δ]
  have hδ₂ : δ.inv ≫ T.map biprod.snd = T.map biprod.snd ≫ α₂.inv := by simp [δ]
  have hγ : γ = δ ≪≫ (δ.symm ≪≫ γ) := by simp
  rw [hγ, of_trans, of_biprod, of_eq_zero_of_inl_comp_eq_of_comp_snd_eq (u := δ.symm ≪≫ γ),
    add_zero]
  · simp [reassoc_of% hδ₁, h₁]
  · simp [h₂, reassoc_of% hδ₂]

end Triangular

section Lift

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] [HasZeroMorphisms C] [HasBinaryBiproducts C]
  {D : Type u'} [Category.{v'} D] (T : C ⥤ D)

/-- An invariant for `K₀(T)` with values in an abelian group `G`: a function on the triples
`(P, α, Q)`, invariant under isomorphisms of triples, additive under binary biproducts and
additive under composition. These are the data that factor through `TauCeti.RelativeK0 T`; see
`TauCeti.RelativeK0.lift`. -/
@[ext]
structure Invariant (G : Type*) [AddCommGroup G] where
  /-- The value of the invariant on a triple. -/
  toFun : ∀ ⦃P Q : C⦄, (T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) → G
  /-- Triples identified by isomorphisms of their objects receive equal values. -/
  map_congr : ∀ ⦃P P' Q Q' : C⦄ (f : P ≅ P') (g : Q ≅ Q') (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q)
    (α' : T.obj P' ≅ T.obj Q'), T.map f.hom ≫ α'.hom = α.hom ≫ T.map g.hom → toFun α = toFun α'
  /-- The value on a direct sum of triples is the sum of the values. -/
  map_biprod : ∀ ⦃P P' Q Q' : C⦄ (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) (α' : T.obj P' ≅ T.obj Q')
    (γ : T.obj (P ⊞ P') ≅ T.obj (Q ⊞ Q')), T.map biprod.inl ≫ γ.hom = α.hom ≫ T.map biprod.inl →
    T.map biprod.inr ≫ γ.hom = α'.hom ≫ T.map biprod.inr → toFun γ = toFun α + toFun α'
  /-- The value on a composite is the sum of the values. -/
  map_trans : ∀ ⦃P Q S : C⦄ (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) (β : T.obj Q ≅ T.obj S),
    toFun (α ≪≫ β) = toFun α + toFun β

variable {T} {G : Type*} [AddCommGroup G]

private lemma Invariant.lift_rel (a : Invariant T G) :
    ∀ r ∈ relativeK0Relations T,
      FreeAddCommGroup.lift (fun p : Σ P Q : C, T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q => a.toFun p.2.2) r = 0 := by
  rintro _ (⟨P, P', Q, Q', f, g, α, α', h, rfl⟩ | ⟨P, P', Q, Q', α, α', γ, h₁, h₂, rfl⟩ |
    ⟨P, Q, S, α, β, rfl⟩)
  · simp [a.map_congr f g α α' h]
  · simp [a.map_biprod α α' γ h₁ h₂]
  · simp [a.map_trans]

/-- The homomorphism out of `K₀(T)` induced by an invariant. -/
noncomputable def lift (a : Invariant T G) : RelativeK0 T →+ G :=
  QuotientAddGroup.lift _
    (FreeAddCommGroup.lift fun p : Σ P Q : C, T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q => a.toFun p.2.2) <|
    (AddSubgroup.closure_le _).2 fun r hr => a.lift_rel r hr

/-- The induced homomorphism sends the class of a triple to the value of the invariant. -/
@[simp]
theorem lift_of (a : Invariant T G) {P Q : C} (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) :
    lift a (of T α) = a.toFun α :=
  (QuotientAddGroup.lift_mk _ _ _).trans (FreeAddCommGroup.lift_apply_of _ _)

/-- The values of a homomorphism out of `K₀(T)` on the classes of triples form an invariant. -/
noncomputable def Invariant.ofHom (f : RelativeK0 T →+ G) : Invariant T G where
  toFun _ _ α := f (of T α)
  map_congr _ _ _ _ u v α α' h := by rw [of_congr u v h]
  map_biprod _ _ _ _ α α' γ h₁ h₂ := by
    rw [of_eq_add_of_inl_comp_eq_of_inr_comp_eq h₁ h₂, map_add]
  map_trans _ _ _ α β := by rw [of_trans, map_add]

/-- The invariant attached to a homomorphism evaluates it on classes of triples. -/
@[simp]
theorem Invariant.ofHom_toFun (f : RelativeK0 T →+ G) {P Q : C} (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) :
    (Invariant.ofHom f).toFun α = f (of T α) := (rfl)

/-- The universal property of `K₀(T)`: invariants with values in `G` correspond bijectively to
homomorphisms `RelativeK0 T →+ G`. -/
noncomputable def liftEquiv : Invariant T G ≃ (RelativeK0 T →+ G) where
  toFun := lift
  invFun := Invariant.ofHom
  left_inv a := by
    ext P Q α
    simp
  right_inv f := by
    ext P Q α
    simp

/-- The universal bijection sends an invariant to the homomorphism it induces. -/
@[simp]
theorem liftEquiv_apply (a : Invariant T G) : liftEquiv a = lift a := (rfl)

/-- The inverse of the universal bijection restricts a homomorphism to classes of triples. -/
@[simp]
theorem liftEquiv_symm_apply (f : RelativeK0 T →+ G) : liftEquiv.symm f = Invariant.ofHom f :=
  (rfl)

end Lift

section FullyFaithful

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] [HasZeroMorphisms C] [HasBinaryBiproducts C]
  {D : Type u'} [Category.{v'} D] (T : C ⥤ D) [T.Full] [T.Faithful]

/-- For a fully faithful functor every triple has trivial class, since every isomorphism
`T(P) ≅ T(Q)` is the image of an isomorphism `P ≅ Q`. -/
theorem of_eq_zero_of_full_of_faithful {P Q : C} (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) : of T α = 0 := by
  have : T.mapIso (T.preimageIso α) = α := by
    ext
    simp
  rw [← this, of_mapIso]

/-- The relative group of a fully faithful functor is trivial; in particular `K₀(𝟭 C) = 0`. -/
instance subsingleton_of_full_of_faithful : Subsingleton (RelativeK0 T) := by
  refine ⟨fun x y => ?_⟩
  suffices h : AddMonoidHom.id (RelativeK0 T) = 0 from
    (DFunLike.congr_fun h x).trans (DFunLike.congr_fun h y).symm
  ext P Q α
  simpa using of_eq_zero_of_full_of_faithful T α

end FullyFaithful

section SplitK0

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] [HasZeroMorphisms C] [HasBinaryBiproducts C]
  [EssentiallySmall.{w} C] {D : Type u'} [Category.{v'} D] (T : C ⥤ D)

/-- The difference map `K₀(T) → K₀(C)`, sending `[P, α, Q]` to `[P] - [Q]` in the split
Grothendieck group of `C`. -/
noncomputable def toSplitK0 : RelativeK0 T →+ SplitK0 C :=
  lift
    { toFun := fun P Q _ => SplitK0.of P - SplitK0.of Q
      map_congr := fun _ _ _ _ f g _ _ _ => by rw [SplitK0.of_congr f, SplitK0.of_congr g]
      map_biprod := fun _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ => by
        rw [SplitK0.of_biprod, SplitK0.of_biprod]
        abel
      map_trans := fun _ _ _ _ _ => by abel }

/-- The difference map sends `[P, α, Q]` to `[P] - [Q]`. -/
@[simp]
theorem toSplitK0_of {P Q : C} (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) :
    toSplitK0 T (of T α) = SplitK0.of P - SplitK0.of Q :=
  lift_of _ α

/-- When `T` sends every object to a zero object, the class of the unique triple `(P, α, 0)` is
additive in `P`; this is the inverse of the difference map. -/
private noncomputable def ofSplitK0OfIsZero [HasZeroObject C] (hT : ∀ P : C, IsZero (T.obj P)) :
    SplitK0 C →+ RelativeK0 T :=
  SplitK0.lift
    { obj := fun P => of T ((hT P).iso (hT 0))
      map_iso := fun _ _ e => of_congr e (Iso.refl 0) ((hT _).eq_of_src _ _)
      map_biprod := fun P P' => by
        rw [of_congr (Iso.refl _) (isoBiprodZero (isZero_zero C))
          (α' := (hT _).iso (hT _)) ((hT _).eq_of_src _ _)]
        exact of_eq_add_of_inl_comp_eq_of_inr_comp_eq ((hT P).eq_of_src _ _)
          ((hT P').eq_of_src _ _) }

private lemma ofSplitK0OfIsZero_of [HasZeroObject C] (hT : ∀ P : C, IsZero (T.obj P)) (P : C) :
    ofSplitK0OfIsZero T hT (SplitK0.of P) = of T ((hT P).iso (hT 0)) :=
  SplitK0.lift_of _ P

/-- When `T` sends every object to a zero object, the difference map is an isomorphism
`K₀(T) ≅ K₀(C)`, whose inverse sends `[P]` to the class of the unique triple `(P, α, 0)`.
For base change along `R → R/R = 0` this is `K₀(R, R) ≅ K₀(R)`. -/
noncomputable def toSplitK0EquivOfIsZero [HasZeroObject C] (hT : ∀ P : C, IsZero (T.obj P)) :
    RelativeK0 T ≃+ SplitK0 C :=
  AddMonoidHom.toAddEquiv (toSplitK0 T) (ofSplitK0OfIsZero T hT)
    (by
      ext P Q α
      -- `α` is the unique isomorphism, the composite of the triples `(P, ·, 0)` and `(0, ·, Q)`.
      have hα : α = (hT P).iso (hT 0) ≪≫ ((hT Q).iso (hT 0)).symm :=
        Iso.ext ((hT P).eq_of_src _ _)
      simp [ofSplitK0OfIsZero_of, hα])
    (by
      ext P
      simp [ofSplitK0OfIsZero_of])

/-- The isomorphism `toSplitK0EquivOfIsZero` is the difference map. -/
@[simp]
theorem toSplitK0EquivOfIsZero_apply [HasZeroObject C] (hT : ∀ P : C, IsZero (T.obj P))
    (x : RelativeK0 T) : toSplitK0EquivOfIsZero T hT x = toSplitK0 T x := (rfl)

/-- The inverse of `toSplitK0EquivOfIsZero` sends `[P]` to the class of the unique triple
`(P, α, 0)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem toSplitK0EquivOfIsZero_symm_of [HasZeroObject C] (hT : ∀ P : C, IsZero (T.obj P))
    (P : C) :
    (toSplitK0EquivOfIsZero T hT).symm (SplitK0.of P) = of T ((hT P).iso (hT 0)) :=
  ofSplitK0OfIsZero_of T hT P

end SplitK0

section MapTriple

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {D : Type u'} [Category.{v'} D] {T : C ⥤ D}
  {C' : Type u''} [Category.{v''} C'] {D' : Type u'''} [Category.{v'''} D'] {T' : C' ⥤ D'}

/-- The image of a triple under a commuting square `e : T ⋙ G ≅ F ⋙ T'`. -/
private noncomputable def mapTriple (G : D ⥤ D') {F : C ⥤ C'} (e : T ⋙ G ≅ F ⋙ T') {P Q : C}
    (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) : T'.obj (F.obj P) ≅ T'.obj (F.obj Q) :=
  (e.app P).symm ≪≫ G.mapIso α ≪≫ e.app Q

/-- A square `T(i) ≫ γ = α ≫ T(j)` of triples is carried by a commuting square of functors to the
square `T'(F(i)) ≫ γ' = α' ≫ T'(F(j))` of their images. -/
private lemma map_map_comp_mapTriple (G : D ⥤ D') {F : C ⥤ C'} (e : T ⋙ G ≅ F ⋙ T')
    {X Y X' Y' : C} {i : X ⟶ X'} {j : Y ⟶ Y'} {α : T.obj X ≅ T.obj Y}
    {γ : T.obj X' ≅ T.obj Y'} (h : T.map i ≫ γ.hom = α.hom ≫ T.map j) :
    T'.map (F.map i) ≫ (mapTriple G e γ).hom = (mapTriple G e α).hom ≫ T'.map (F.map j) := by
  have h₁ := e.inv.naturality i
  have h₂ := e.hom.naturality j
  simp only [Functor.comp_map] at h₁ h₂
  simp only [mapTriple, Iso.trans_hom, Iso.symm_hom, Iso.app_inv, Iso.app_hom,
    Functor.mapIso_hom, reassoc_of% h₁, ← G.map_comp_assoc, h, G.map_comp, Category.assoc, h₂]

/-- The square of `map_map_comp_mapTriple`, transported along isomorphisms `a : F(X') ≅ A` and
`b : F(Y') ≅ B` carrying `F(i)` to `i'` and `F(j)` to `j'`. -/
private lemma map_comp_mapTriple_conj (G : D ⥤ D') {F : C ⥤ C'} (e : T ⋙ G ≅ F ⋙ T')
    {X Y X' Y' : C} {A B : C'} {i : X ⟶ X'} {j : Y ⟶ Y'} {i' : F.obj X ⟶ A} {j' : F.obj Y ⟶ B}
    (a : F.obj X' ≅ A) (b : F.obj Y' ≅ B) (hi : F.map i ≫ a.hom = i') (hj : F.map j ≫ b.hom = j')
    {α : T.obj X ≅ T.obj Y} {γ : T.obj X' ≅ T.obj Y'} (h : T.map i ≫ γ.hom = α.hom ≫ T.map j) :
    T'.map i' ≫ ((T'.mapIso a).symm ≪≫ mapTriple G e γ ≪≫ T'.mapIso b).hom =
      (mapTriple G e α).hom ≫ T'.map j' := by
  subst hi hj
  simp [reassoc_of% map_map_comp_mapTriple G e h]

end MapTriple

section Map

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] [HasZeroMorphisms C] [HasBinaryBiproducts C]
  {D : Type u'} [Category.{v'} D] {T : C ⥤ D}
  {C' : Type u''} [Category.{v''} C'] [HasZeroMorphisms C'] [HasBinaryBiproducts C']
  {D' : Type u'''} [Category.{v'''} D'] {T' : C' ⥤ D'}

/-- The homomorphism `K₀(T) → K₀(T')` induced by a square of functors `F : C ⥤ C'`,
`G : D ⥤ D'` commuting up to the specified isomorphism `e : T ⋙ G ≅ F ⋙ T'`. It sends
`[P, α, Q]` to `[F(P), e⁻¹ ≫ G(α) ≫ e, F(Q)]`. -/
noncomputable def map (F : C ⥤ C') [F.PreservesZeroMorphisms]
    [PreservesBiproductsOfShape WalkingPair F] (G : D ⥤ D') (e : T ⋙ G ≅ F ⋙ T') :
    RelativeK0 T →+ RelativeK0 T' :=
  have := preservesBinaryBiproducts_of_preservesBiproducts F
  lift
    { toFun := fun _ _ α => of T' (mapTriple G e α)
      map_congr := fun _ _ _ _ f g _ _ h =>
        of_congr (F.mapIso f) (F.mapIso g) (map_map_comp_mapTriple G e h)
      map_biprod := fun P P' Q Q' α α' γ h₁ h₂ => by
        -- Transport the image of `γ` along `F(P ⊞ P') ≅ F(P) ⊞ F(P')` and
        -- `F(Q ⊞ Q') ≅ F(Q) ⊞ F(Q')`, where `F` of the inclusions become the inclusions.
        rw [of_congr (F.mapBiprod P P') (F.mapBiprod Q Q')
          (α' := (T'.mapIso (F.mapBiprod P P')).symm ≪≫ mapTriple G e γ ≪≫
            T'.mapIso (F.mapBiprod Q Q'))
          (by simp only [Iso.trans_hom, Iso.symm_hom, Functor.mapIso_hom, Functor.mapIso_inv,
            Iso.hom_inv_id_map_assoc])]
        exact of_eq_add_of_inl_comp_eq_of_inr_comp_eq
          (map_comp_mapTriple_conj G e _ _ (by simp) (by simp) h₁)
          (map_comp_mapTriple_conj G e _ _ (by simp) (by simp) h₂)
      map_trans := fun _ _ _ α β => by
        rw [← of_trans]
        congr 1
        ext
        simp [mapTriple] }

/-- The map induced by a commuting square sends `[P, α, Q]` to `[F(P), e⁻¹ ≫ G(α) ≫ e, F(Q)]`. -/
@[simp]
theorem map_of (F : C ⥤ C') [F.PreservesZeroMorphisms]
    [PreservesBiproductsOfShape WalkingPair F] (G : D ⥤ D') (e : T ⋙ G ≅ F ⋙ T') {P Q : C}
    (α : T.obj P ≅ T.obj Q) :
    map F G e (of T α) = of T' ((e.app P).symm ≪≫ G.mapIso α ≪≫ e.app Q) :=
  lift_of _ α

/-- The identity square induces the identity of `K₀(T)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem map_id : map (𝟭 C) (𝟭 D) (T.rightUnitor ≪≫ T.leftUnitor.symm) =
    AddMonoidHom.id (RelativeK0 T) := by
  ext P Q α
  rw [map_of, AddMonoidHom.id_apply]
  congr 1
  ext
  simp

/-- The map induced by the pasting of two commuting squares is the composite of their maps. -/
theorem map_comp {C'' : Type*} [Category* C''] [HasZeroMorphisms C''] [HasBinaryBiproducts C'']
    {D'' : Type*} [Category* D''] {T'' : C'' ⥤ D''} (F₁ : C ⥤ C') [F₁.PreservesZeroMorphisms]
    [PreservesBiproductsOfShape WalkingPair F₁] (G₁ : D ⥤ D') (e₁ : T ⋙ G₁ ≅ F₁ ⋙ T')
    (F₂ : C' ⥤ C'') [F₂.PreservesZeroMorphisms] [PreservesBiproductsOfShape WalkingPair F₂]
    (G₂ : D' ⥤ D'') (e₂ : T' ⋙ G₂ ≅ F₂ ⋙ T'') :
    map (F₁ ⋙ F₂) (G₁ ⋙ G₂) ((Functor.associator _ _ _).symm ≪≫ Functor.isoWhiskerRight e₁ G₂ ≪≫
      Functor.associator _ _ _ ≪≫ Functor.isoWhiskerLeft F₁ e₂ ≪≫
        (Functor.associator _ _ _).symm) = (map F₂ G₂ e₂).comp (map F₁ G₁ e₁) := by
  ext P Q α
  rw [AddMonoidHom.comp_apply, map_of, map_of, map_of]
  congr 1
  ext
  simp

/-- The map induced by a commuting square is compatible with the difference maps:
`[F(P)] - [F(Q)]` is the image of `[P] - [Q]` under the map of split `K₀` induced by `F`. -/
theorem toSplitK0_comp_map [EssentiallySmall.{w} C] [EssentiallySmall.{w'} C'] (F : C ⥤ C')
    [F.PreservesZeroMorphisms] [PreservesBiproductsOfShape WalkingPair F] (G : D ⥤ D')
    (e : T ⋙ G ≅ F ⋙ T') :
    (toSplitK0 T').comp (map F G e) = (SplitK0.map F).comp (toSplitK0 T) := by
  ext P Q α
  simp

end Map

end RelativeK0

end TauCeti
